<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marienkirche, Gelnhausen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th–13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Marienkirche in Gelnhausen, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, is a late Romanesque and early Gothic church built mainly in the 12th and 13th centuries. Its unusual group of towers at the east end, its carved rood screen and its rich decoration make it one of the outstanding buildings of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> period in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p></div>
